From d7cd6331140e3b4685d13dbc06005d0a34c7c559 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: stephan-xyz <stephan@zehrer.net>
Date: Wed, 25 Nov 2026 18:01:38 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 28/29] xhcid: a done command TRB keeps its cycle bit (#749)

The IRQ reactor overwrote each completed command TRB with a Reserved
TRB with cycle bit 0. On the first lap of the command ring (producer
cycle 1) such an entry is not owned by the xHC, but after the ring
wraps the consumer cycle is 0, and every done entry ahead of the new
commands was owned: the xHC ran them as invalid TRBs, completed each
with TRB Error, and the commands queued after the wrap never completed,
so xhcid hung. On the Pi 400 this happened after 255 commands, with a
replugged USB device or with No Op commands alone (pi-tests Tests 663,
665, 666). Transfer rings were not affected: their TRBs are not cleared.

Keep the TRB's own cycle bit when marking it done, so it is not owned
on the next lap.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 drivers/usb/xhcid/src/xhci/irq_reactor.rs | 9 ++++++++-
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/usb/xhcid/src/xhci/irq_reactor.rs b/drivers/usb/xhcid/src/xhci/irq_reactor.rs
index e2be0c93..13a97e1e 100644
--- a/drivers/usb/xhcid/src/xhci/irq_reactor.rs
+++ b/drivers/usb/xhcid/src/xhci/irq_reactor.rs
@@ -451,7 +451,14 @@ impl<const N: usize> IrqReactor<N> {
                         {
                             Some(command_trb) => {
                                 let t = command_trb.clone();
-                                command_trb.reserved(false);
+                                // Mark it done, but keep its cycle bit. With
+                                // cycle 0 a done entry was owned by the xHC on
+                                // every second lap of the ring: after the first
+                                // wrap (consumer cycle 0) the xHC ran all of
+                                // them as invalid TRBs, one TRB Error each,
+                                // and the commands queued after the wrap never
+                                // completed (pi-tests Tests 663, 665, 666).
+                                command_trb.reserved(t.cycle());
                                 t
                             }
                             None => {
